{
  "_comment": "Note footer split contract (Spec #234 R11-R13; ruling D13; WI #238). Each split row: `on` names the splitters it runs through: `daily` = Rust memex_core::daily::split_body and Dart splitDailyBody; `note` = Rust memex_core::daily::split_note_body and Dart splitNoteBody. Each must return exactly `person`, `chips` and `tags` for `input`. A footer tag line is a line below the marker starting with `#` and then a character other than a space or `#`; writes drop it (rows decide the footer), and its name, as written after `#` with trailing spaces and CR trimmed, is reported in `tags`. Other non-chip lines below the marker are stray text, moved to the end of the person section. `decision` groups rows: every decision WI #238's AC names keeps at least one row. Each assemble row: Rust daily::assemble(person, chips) and Dart assembleDailyBody(person, chips) return exactly `body`.",
  "marker": "<!-- memex:topics -->",
  "split": [
    {
      "decision": "chip line",
      "name": "a chip line becomes a chip",
      "on": [
        "daily",
        "note"
      ],
      "input": "Day.\n<!-- memex:topics -->\n[[Player Loop~about]]\n",
      "person": "Day.\n",
      "chips": [
        "Player Loop"
      ],
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "decision": "tag line",
      "name": "tag lines after the chips are dropped and reported",
      "on": [
        "daily",
        "note"
      ],
      "input": "Day.\n<!-- memex:topics -->\n[[Player Loop~about]]\n#work\n#q3-plan\n",
      "person": "Day.\n",
      "chips": [
        "Player Loop"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "work",
        "q3-plan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "decision": "tag line",
      "name": "a tag line before a chip line is still a tag line",
      "on": [
        "daily",
        "note"
      ],
      "input": "Day.\n<!-- memex:topics -->\n#work\n[[Player Loop~about]]\n",
      "person": "Day.\n",
      "chips": [
        "Player Loop"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "work"
      ]
    },
    {
      "decision": "legacy tag line",
      "name": "a legacy name with a space is one tag line",
      "on": [
        "daily",
        "note"
      ],
      "input": "Day.\n<!-- memex:topics -->\n#My Tag\n",
      "person": "Day.\n",
      "chips": [],
      "tags": [
        "My Tag"
      ]
    },
    {
      "decision": "legacy tag line",
